From b867a4e93181a364c3c5ee5be3d2163e6afd40f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaorenex1 <24537608z@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:55:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a session-scoped plugin control bridge

Plugins see a session id in every hook payload but never the agent, so a
background reviewer has no way to steer the live turn. hermes_cli.plugin_runtime
binds the running agent for the duration of run_conversation and exposes steer
(queue text at the next safe boundary), a one-slot turn continuation queue with an
observable token, and a read-only turn_state probe.

The advice is queued through a new steer(kind="adviser") path and delivered as a
display_kind=adviser row, not the operator /steer frame: a reviewer's advice must
not claim the user's authority. redirect() is deliberately not used because it
persists a user correction.
